		(title "RP2040-Zero-Pico-Debug-Adapter")
		(company "Generated by Codex")
		(comment 1 "Waveshare RP2040-Zero debugprobe-zero adapter for Raspberry Pi Pico targets")
		(comment 2 "Target 3V3 is intentionally not connected")
	)
	(lib_symbols)
	(text_box "Electrical schematic / net map\n\nRP2040-Zero module headers:\n  GP10 -> R1 47R -> Pico SWD JST-SH pin 1 SWCLK\n  GND  ----------------> Pico SWD JST-SH pin 2 GND\n  GP11 -> R2 47R -> Pico SWD JST-SH pin 3 SWDIO\n\n  GP4  -> R3 47R -> UART JST-SH pin 1 TX from probe\n  GND  ----------------> UART JST-SH pin 2 GND\n  GP5  -> R4 47R -> UART JST-SH pin 3 RX to probe\n\n  GP12 -> R5 47R -> optional RUN/RESET header pin 1 and TP1\n  GND  ----------------> optional RUN/RESET header pin 2\n\nNo RP2040-Zero 3V3 net is routed to the target connectors by default.\nAll series resistors are through-hole and may be populated as 47 ohm parts or replaced with jumpers.\nJ1/J2 are the RP2040-Zero mounting headers. Verify module orientation before soldering."
